{"login":"myers","id":12242,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMjQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12242?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myers","html_url":"https://github.com/myers","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myers/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myers/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myers/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myers/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myers/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myers/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-05T19:00:10Z","updated_at":"2026-06-05T19:00:10Z","body":"@fanninpm \n> What tests would fail when `EllipsisType` is absent?\n\nI think I updated the description after the first post with that info: `test_json.test_default::test_bad_default`","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/comments/4634586012/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/comments/4634858342","html_url":"https://github.com/RustPython/RustPython/issues/8052#issuecomment-4634858342","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/8052","id":4634858342,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCA8Bec8AAAABFEJTZg","user":{"login":"fanninpm","id":27117322,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MTE3MzIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27117322?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fanninpm","html_url":"https://github.com/fanninpm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fanninpm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fanninpm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fanninpm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fanninpm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fanninpm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fanninpm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fanninpm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fanninpm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fanninpm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-05T19:34:42Z","updated_at":"2026-06-05T19:34:42Z","body":"I think I misunderstood the first time. To be clear, `EllipsisType` is supposed to be defined in `Lib/types.py` and nowhere else, correct?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/comments/4634858342/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/comments/4643392382","html_url":"https://github.com/RustPython/RustPython/issues/8052#issuecomment-4643392382","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/8052","id":4643392382,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCA8Bec8AAAABFMSLfg","user":{"login":"myers","id":12242,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMjQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12242?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myers","html_url":"https://github.com/myers","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myers/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myers/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myers/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myers/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myers/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myers/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-07T17:24:16Z","updated_at":"2026-06-07T17:24:16Z","body":"Let me lay out exactly where each piece lives, since \"defined\" splits into two things — the type vs. the EllipsisType name — and RustPython mirrors CPython here.\n\nThe type itself (whose `__name__/tp_name` is \"ellipsis\", lowercase):\n- CPython: Objects/sliceobject.c — PyEllipsis_Type, tp_name = \"ellipsis\".\n- RustPython: crates/vm/src/builtins/slice.rs — `#[pyclass(... name = \"EllipsisType\")]`. This name is the bug — it should be \"ellipsis\".\n\nThe EllipsisType name is never a type — it's just an alias to that type, exposed by the types module. On both interpreters Lib/types.py does `from _types import *` first, with a pure-Python fallback:\n\n- CPython: the C module Modules/_typesmodule.c provides EllipsisType; fallback is EllipsisType = type(Ellipsis) in Lib/types.py.\n- RustPython: the native module crates/vm/src/stdlib/_types.rs provides EllipsisType (→ ctx.types.ellipsis_type); same type(Ellipsis) fallback in Lib/types.py.\n- Lib/_collections_abc.py also binds EllipsisType = type(...) — on both, for internal use.\n\nSo to your question: no, it isn't \"in types.py and nowhere else\" — but every occurrence is an alias computed from the object (type(Ellipsis) / ctx.types.ellipsis_type), not a lookup of the type's __name__. That's why the fix is just renaming the builtin's name to \"ellipsis\": types.EllipsisType is type(...) stays True everywhere, and only __name__/repr change — to match CPython.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/comments/4643392382/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/comments/4889084776","html_url":"https://github.com/RustPython/RustPython/issues/8052#issuecomment-4889084776","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/8052","id":4889084776,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCA8Bec8AAAABI2mDaA","user":{"login":"shAn-kor","id":53287605,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMjg3NjA1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53287605?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shAn-kor","html_url":"https://github.com/shAn-kor","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shAn-kor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shAn-kor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shAn-kor/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shAn-kor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shAn-kor/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shAn-kor/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shAn-kor/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shAn-kor/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shAn-kor/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-06T04:29:04Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T04:29:04Z","body":"I’m interested in working on this issue. Is it okay if I take it?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/comments/4889084776/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/comments/4939